Additional Per-Language Test Data Attributions
==============================================

- Wikipedia-derived vocabularies (armenian, basque, catalan, czech, esperanto,
  estonian, finnish, french, greek, hindi, indonesian, italian, lithuanian,
  persian, sesotho, tamil, ukrainian):
  Include word lists extracted from Wikimedia/Wikipedia dumps licensed under
  CC BY-SA 3.0 / 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/).

- arabic.tsv.gz:
  Derived from the "Arabic Wordlist for Spellchecking" v1.6 by Mohammed Attia
  (https://sourceforge.net/projects/arabic-wordlist/), licensed under GPLv3+.

- polish.tsv.gz:
  Derived from the Wortschatz Leipzig Polish corpus
  (https://wortschatz.uni-leipzig.de/en/download/Polish), CC BY 4.0.

- serbian.tsv.gz:
  Derived from the srWaC Serbian web corpus (http://nlp.ffzg.hr/resources/corpora/srwac/),
  CC BY-SA.

- yiddish.tsv.gz:
  Derived from the YIVO Yiddish spellchecker dictionary by Simcha Taub
  (http://yiddish-sources.com/yiddish-spell-checker).
